ent all of my IEP doing this research  and so I didn't take any other classes  or any units that I needed towards  graduation so in the spring everything  was kind of jus the independent study  all the courses and and and all of that  so it was difficult but I mean I worked  with Anjali a lot and trying to figure  out how I needed to craft the paper and  so we did a few you know iterations of  that she actually is very hands-on so  she will take post-it notes and write  you know this safer section could be  this do you agree what are you trying to  get from there so she kind of pushed me  a bit and ask me questions that help me  figure out the structure of the paper  and also the time I would spend on each  section and what was more important and  what was less important and how I you  know like just I could show that I  actually did the work so you know  because doing the work and actually  reporting the work is quite different  but yeah in the end it worked  definitely with Anthony's help and you  know working extra hours  so I think this experience was  interesting for me because I ended up  using frameworks in in the independent  study that I think are unique to Sloane  so for example I used the I used systems  thinking which is you know obviously a  big thing here at Sloane and also kind  of things around sustainability and  sustainability oriented innovation which  is MIT which MIT is you know a champion  in so I think that being in this  environment kind of helped kind of  helped with the the framework so I was  gonna use and the the way I was writing  this paper enterpreneurship is also big  at MIT so that's why I even wants to be  an entrepreneur after a 10-year career  in finance so I think all of those  things kind of work together to to help  me produce this independent study I do  think however it's you know it's it's  just yes for me it was MIT but for  anyone else it could be anything right  it's just a matter of figuring out what  you have in your own ecosystem and then  using that to your advantage  also in addition to being Aslam  negative fellow which is Legatum is a  center here and my MIT for  entrepreneurship and development and it  supports 20 fellows per year that wants  to work in the developing world after  graduation so it's everybody from PhDs  in engineering to you know undergraduate  and so I came here through a scholarship  from the Legatum Foundation so it helped  me so I knew coming in that I wanted to  be an entrepreneur in the developing  world after Sloane so you know and my  startup idea is in agriculture so it  kind of you know it's another part of  what what created this independent study  I knew some people that I interviewed in  the you know that I interviewed some  stakeholders that I interviewed truly  got'em and then approaching them as Alec  Adam fellow it kind of made sense that I  was doing this you know agriculture  paper so it kind of helped me you know  talk to people that I probably would  never had time reaching out to Angela  also brought in her contacts for people  that I needed to interview so that was  helpful as well and and the name MIT was  helpful as well so I guess to kind of  link back to the ecosystem right so  reaching out to someone is saying hey  I'm a student at MIT and I'm studying  this topic was I think helpful for  people to open up their doors and and  resources and such  I just came from a conference last week  after graduation I went straight to a  conference at the World Bank and it's  just this I think everybody is kind of  questioning this idea of does technology  actually is technology a good solution  and if so how should we be using it and  how do we really get this rural  communities to to prosper you know and  there's a lot actually in between  farming seasons right so you know  farming season could be just three  months or you know and then you add the  the preparation time which is another  couple of months and then you know  farmers are going 